# ORCLROOM: quit/debug/help prompt parity (M16.7a). Oracle-verifies the three
# modal prompt shapes this fork keeps interactive-only per M1.4/M3.9/M3.11:
# GamePromptEndPlay's SidebarPromptYesNo line, GameDebugPrompt's PromptString
# text-entry field, and the 'H' help window (TextWindowDisplayFile). See
# NOTES.md/oracle_parity_test.go for why the title screen's high-score DISPLAY
# ('H' on the monitor) has no scenario here: it is drawn only by the
# terminal-only GameTitleLoop, never reached by GameStepWithInputs or the
# protocol.
world ORCLROOM
seed 0
boot 240
play
move right
capture baseline
key 63 35
key 65 1E
key 77 32
key 77 32
key 79 18
capture debug_typed
key 13 1C
capture debug_applied
key 81 10
capture quit_open
key 78 31
capture quit_cancelled
move right
capture quit_resumes
key 72 23
capture help_open
key 27 01
capture help_closed
